<Base title="About — Erasto Wanjau">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Erasto Wanjau, a data scientist and software developer based in Nairobi. I work across
    the full arc of a data problem: framing the question, cleaning and understanding the data,
    building the model or dashboard, and communicating the result so someone can act on it.
  </p>

  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p>
    My roots are in software engineering — I trained as a full-stack engineer at ALX, building
    systems in Python, C, and shell — and that shapes how I do data science. I care about
    pipelines that are reproducible, code that is modular, and analyses that state their
    assumptions out loud. Before a model makes a claim, the data behind it has earned the
    right to make one.
  </p>

  <h2>Selected projects</h2>
  <p>
    The case studies on this site cover hospital pharmacy analytics in Power BI, an
    end-to-end real-estate price pipeline, statistical analysis of Tanzanian water-point data,
    and a World Cup predictor that grew into a full Streamlit application. The rest of my
    work — including SQL analytics, the Latin America housing series, and earlier engineering
    projects — is on <a href="https://github.com/EWanjau">GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Writing</h2>
  <p>
    I write about what I'm learning on <a href="https://dev.to/erasto">dev.to</a> — see the
    <a href="/writing/">Writing page</a> for the latest.
  </p>

